> **You are building a local web application that replicates the BMB Ultimate Dispute Letter Generator pipeline. The app takes uploaded credit report images and produces a complete downloadable dispute package. Here is the full spec:**

>
> **PIPELINE (replicate exactly):**
> 1. User uploads 1–10 credit report images (JPG/PNG/PDF) via a drag-and-drop UI
> 2. Backend sends images to the Anthropic API (`claude-sonnet-4-6`) with the full BMB system prompt — all 15 project knowledge files concatenated as the system context, plus the uploaded images as user content
> 3. Claude analyzes the report, runs the 33-point Metro 2 audit, identifies all violations by furnisher
> 4. Backend uses the `docx` npm package to generate: one dispute letter per furnisher (addressed to the CRA, CC-ing the furnisher), a standalone File Disclosure letter, a Highlighting Guide, and Mailing Instructions — all as `.docx` files
> 5. Backend generates an interactive HTML violation report
> 6. All files are zipped together and served as one download
>
> **UI REQUIREMENTS:**
> - Clean dark-themed dashboard (dark navy header, white cards)
> - Step indicator: Upload → Analyzing → Generating → Download
> - Progress bar during API call
> - Violation summary cards (total, critical, high, medium) shown before download
> - Download button for full ZIP + individual file links
> - Error states with clear messages
>
> **FILE STRUCTURE TO CREATE:**
> ```
> bmb-webapp/
>   server.js          ← Express server, API calls, docx generation, zip
>   public/
>     index.html       ← Single page app
>     style.css
>     app.js
>   knowledge/         ← All 15 BMB project knowledge files go here
>   uploads/           ← Temp storage for uploaded images
>   outputs/           ← Generated files per session
>   package.json
> ```
>
> **KEY DEPENDENCIES to install:**
> `express`, `multer` (file uploads), `docx` (Word doc generation), `archiver` (ZIP), `@anthropic-ai/sdk`, `dotenv`
>
> **ANTHROPIC API CALL PATTERN:**
> - Model: `claude-sonnet-4-6`
> - Load all files in the `knowledge/` folder as text and concatenate into the system prompt
> - Send uploaded images as base64 in the user message
> - Use the exact BMB Power Prompt from the Operating Protocol as the user message text
> - Parse the response to extract violations by furnisher, then feed that structured data into the docx generators
>
> **ENV FILE needed:** Create `.env` with `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_key_here`
>
> **The docx letter format must match exactly:** VIA CERTIFIED MAIL header block, CRA address, RE line, CC block with furnisher address and tracking number blank, consumer info block, numbered violations with statute citations, 8 statutory demands (A–H), compliance timeline, certification and signature block.
>
> Build the complete working application. Start with `server.js` and `package.json`, then the frontend, then test end-to-end with a sample run. Make sure `node server.js` starts the app on port 3000 with no errors.

